---
import { DMG_SIZE, MIN_MACOS, REPO, VERSION } from "../data/release";
---

<section class="press" id="press" aria-labelledby="press-title" data-shot="press">
  <div class="wrap press-grid">
    <header class="press-head">
      <p class="label kicker">Press conference</p>
      <h2 class="poster" id="press-title" data-reveal>Questions from the press.</h2>
      <p class="sub" data-reveal style="--i: 1">Unlike some, we answer them.</p>
    </header>

    <dl class="qa">
      <div class="item">
        <dt>Is this a joke?</dt>
        <dd>
          The name is. The browser isn’t: it’s a full Chromium browser with the extensions, passwords and codecs you’d
          expect. The satire is aimed at Benjamin Netanyahu and his government’s politics, and at nobody else.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="item" id="install">
        <dt>macOS won’t open it.</dt>
        <dd>
          <p>
            Version {VERSION} is signed with a Developer ID but not yet notarized by Apple, so Gatekeeper blocks the
            first launch. Once:
          </p>
          <ol>
            <li>Open the DMG and drag Netnyahoo into Applications.</li>
            <li>Open Netnyahoo. macOS refuses; click Done.</li>
            <li>Go to System Settings › Privacy &amp; Security, scroll down, and click <b>Open Anyway</b>.</li>
          </ol>
          <p>Or, in Terminal:</p>
          <pre><code>xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/Netnyahoo.app</code></pre>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <dt>Will it run on my Mac?</dt>
        <dd>
          If it has Apple Silicon (M1 or later) and runs {MIN_MACOS} or later, yes. There’s no Intel build. The
          download is {DMG_SIZE}.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <dt>What doesn’t it do yet?</dt>
        <dd>
          Sync, Translate, and Widevine DRM, so Netflix and other protected video won’t play. Passkeys stored in iCloud
          Keychain are waiting on an entitlement from Apple; Touch ID and phone passkeys work. There’s no AI assistant.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <dt>Does it update itself?</dt>
        <dd>The app updates through Sparkle with signed releases. Extensions update themselves through the Web Store.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <dt>What does it collect?</dt>
        <dd>
          Nothing. The app has no analytics, and Chromium’s crash reporting and usage pings are compiled out. The sites
          you visit, the extensions you install and your search engine see what they always see. Google is the default
          search engine until you change it; nobody paid for that.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <dt>Is this Dia?</dt>
        <dd>
          No. The interface follows Dia’s closely. Netnyahoo has nothing to do with The Browser Company, which has not
          been asked for its opinion and would probably rather not give one.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <dt>Is it really open source?</dt>
        <dd>
          All of it, including the Chromium patches, is on <a class="link" href={REPO} rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.
          Issues and pull requests are welcome; so is a fork.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <dt>Why “Netnyahoo”?</dt>
        <dd>Because a browser should do what it’s told and leave when asked. Some offices could take notes.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .press {
    padding-top: var(--section);
  }
  .press-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(12, minmax(0, 1fr));
    column-gap: var(--gutter);
    row-gap: 48px;
  }
  .press-head {
    grid-column: 1 / span 5;
    align-self: start;
    position: sticky;
    top: 100px;
  }
  .kicker {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 1.2rem + 4vw, 5.6rem);
  }
  .sub {
    margin-top: 20px;
    font-size: var(--t-lede);
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .qa {
    grid-column: 7 / -1;
    margin: 0;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .item {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.4rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    padding: 24px 0 26px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  dt,
  dd {
    grid-column: 2;
  }
  dt {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 560;
    font-size: 1.28rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    position: relative;
  }
  dt::before,
  dd::before {
    position: absolute;
    left: -2.4rem;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: var(--t-label);
    font-stretch: 87.5%;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    line-height: 2.2;
  }
  dt::before {
    content: "Q.";
  }
  dd {
    margin: 10px 0 0;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    position: relative;
  }
  dd::before {
    content: "A.";
    top: 0;
  }
  dd > * + * {
    margin-top: 12px;
  }
  ol {
    margin-block: 12px;
    padding-left: 1.3em;
  }
  li + li {
    margin-top: 4px;
  }
  b {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  pre {
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    padding: 12px 14px;
    background: var(--paper-deep);
    border-radius: 3px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    font-stretch: 87.5%;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .press-head,
    .qa {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
      position: static;
    }
  }
</style>
